            <ArticleTitle>Operative laparoscopy (minimally invasive surgery): state of the art.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In any body cavity, endoscopic surgery is possible and usually preferable. Advantages include better exposure, magnification, and operating very close to the affected tissue. We demonstrate some of the past, present, and future of laparoscopy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
